contrary to this new movement about  ideas and dialogue and platforming and  hearing everybody out I think it's  important at some point to insert what  should be a pretty obvious reality to us  which is that no matter what  conversations you want to have or you  choose to have or you enable the halving  of  you can't find middle ground with crazy  people not every idea deserves to be  part of the discussion not every person  can be part of the solution and some  people and their ideas have to be  ignored have to be kept out of the  discussion or we are going to truly  damage ourselves as a species as a human  society as a country however you want to  slice and dice it now before people go  crazy and start writing in saying David  you're calling for censorship you're  calling for mistreatment of people you  are limiting people's First Amendment  rights and limiting what people have to  say I'm not okay this came up last week  during the interview I did with Joe  Rogan in Los Angeles there's lots of  great things about this movement of the  last several years that says it wants to  hear all ideas and it wants to figure  out what's best and have in-depth  discussion was with people from all  sides of the political spectrum that's  great okay I've been doing it for ten  years on the show dialogue is good  discourse is critical to human  advancement a diverse range of opinions  should be heard and considered and  evaluated when we are trying to figure  out as humans what is best for our  future and what's best for our societies  but there are people out there with  outrageously extreme bad ideas and it's  okay to put the line somewhere and say  you don't get a seat at the table we're  going to figure this thing out without  you because your ideas are terrible and  crazy and dangerous in some cases now of  course the devil is in the details and  who is it that Gates gets that sort of  gatekeeping power that's a real question  but during the Joe Rogan interview I  pointed