he underlying  idea is that we're constantly merging  opposed ideologies that will get us  closer to an ideal or a solution or  perfection of some kind to use a utopian  idealistic term this doesn't work with  outrageous bad faith ignorant or  cognitively limited people and horrible  ideas period we need to stop  going so far into the marketplace of  ideas to the point where it becomes self  destructed by map its destructive rather  when we mandate that all ideas be  considered equally and given equal  footing we are actually ceding ground to  extremism and this is not an  hypothetical this is how the right has  won many victories if eventually the  solution is going to end up as the  midpoint or the average or the mean of  all ideas by presenting the most extreme  possible ideas you pull the average to  your side Republicans know this the  right know this knows this and they've  used it successfully if the debate over  abortion is about up until what point in  a pregnancy should abortion be legal and  we sort of concede that we're going to  end up in the middle of all of the  suggestions that we get the  anti-abortion right is incentivized to  straight up say all abortions should be  illegal at one day of pregnancy abortion  is illegal and if we guarantee that  crazy position a seat at the table they  win by suggesting the craziest possible  idea and pulling the Overton Window  pulling the average of the debate over  to their side if the debate over the  highest marginal tax rate is going to  end up as the average of all the  proposed ideas the right benefits by  saying the tax rate should be zero or  taxation is slavery because it pulls the  average towards them I wish Democrats  had understood this longer ago if they  had decided not to seed a ton of ground  to Republicans trying to negotiate over  things that Republicans simply will not  negotiate about we would be far better  off today if you do a show and you want  to hear out wacky ideas do it I do it on  this show as long as I'm prepared to  responsibly do it pushing back against  them giving an opposing view but when  we're trying to have the serious  conversations we don't have any  responsibility to let just any crazy old  notion into the discussion when a new  plane is being developed there's a  cut-off as to what ideas Boeing or  Airbus allow into the discussion and who  is allowed to contribute to the planes  this  anything else would be ridiculous when  we consider the best treatment for a  medical condition not every crazy notion  is given the same value this is logical  it shouldn't be different with politics  this isn't censorship everyone can say  whatever they want say it on YouTube go  to your local City Council meeting and  say it write a letter to your elected  officials do a podcast whatever but you  can't negotiate with crazy people and  their crazy ideas and they don't have to  be given a seat at the big-boy table and  that's okay period let me know if you  disagree
 

